<section class="sec"><h2 class="h2">Your body isn’t failing you. It’s protecting you.</h2>
<p class="t">Your body&#x27;s stress response is built for short bursts. Cortisol, your main stress hormone, is meant to rise and then fall.</p>
<p class="t">When stress doesn&#x27;t let up for months or years (a divorce, a betrayal, two jobs, caring for everyone), your body stays on alert. And a body on alert holds on.</p>
<p class="t">That&#x27;s why trying harder can feel like it backfires. Cutting food and adding cardio tell an alarmed body there&#x27;s even more to worry about.</p>
<p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#3F5A1E;margin-top:4px">THE LOOP · EACH STEP FEEDS THE NEXT</p>
